# Neo Utility parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoUtility
namespace NeoBuzz.Utility
class NeoUtilityMachine
summary Gain, balance or mono pan, width 0–200 %, bass mono below a frequency, polarity invert per channel, channel swap and DC removal, each exact (gain in 0.1 dB steps), and a mid/side matrix (encode or decode), so any stereo machine between two Utilities works on mid and side. Zero latency; at its defaults it passes the input bit for bit. Use it for gain staging and stereo fixes as one-parameter moves: trim a track, narrow or widen it, make the lows mono, fix a flipped channel, EQ or compress the side alone.

group Level
Gain      "Gain"           0 841   601  db -60.1 24 inf        | Output gain in 0.1 dB steps, −60 … +24 dB (bottom: −∞, silence)
    how Sets the output level from -60 to +24 dB; the bottom of the range is silence.
    sound It makes the sound louder or quieter without changing its tone.
Pan       "Pan"            0 1000  500  bip                    | −100 % left … +100 % right
    how Moves the sound from 100 % left to 100 % right.
    sound The sound shifts across the stereo field.
PanLaw    "Pan law"        0 1     0    enum Balance Mono_pan  | Balance: the far side fades linearly, 0 dB at centre (stereo sources). Mono pan: sums to mono, sine/cosine law, −3 dB per side at centre
    how Chooses Balance, where the far side fades, or Mono pan, which sums to mono and pans with a sine/cosine law.
    sound Balance suits stereo sources; Mono pan suits a single mono source and keeps its loudness even as it moves.
group Stereo
Width     "Width"          0 200   100  lin 0 200 % 0          | Side signal × width: 0 % is mono, 100 % unchanged, 200 % twice the side
    how Scales the side signal, from 0 % (mono) through 100 % (unchanged) to 200 % (twice as wide).
    sound Lower values narrow the sound towards mono; higher values make it broader.
BassMono  "Bass mono"      0 1     0    switch                 | Makes everything below Bass mono freq mono
    how Makes everything below Bass mono freq mono.
    sound The bass is centred and solid, which helps on small speakers and in clubs.
BassFreq  "Bass mono freq" 0 10000 5566 freq 20 500            | Below this the side signal is removed (4th-order Butterworth high-pass, −3 dB here)
    how Sets the frequency, from 20 to 500 Hz, below which the sound is made mono.
    sound Higher values centre more of the low end, lower values keep more of it wide.
group Channels
InvertL   "Invert L"       0 1     0    switch                 | Flips the polarity of the left input (before Swap)
    how Flips the polarity of the left input.
    sound The left channel is upside down, which can fix thin, phasey sound when two sources cancel.
InvertR   "Invert R"       0 1     0    switch                 | Flips the polarity of the right input (before Swap)
    how Flips the polarity of the right input.
    sound The right channel is upside down, which can fix thin, phasey sound when two sources cancel.
Swap      "Swap"           0 1     0    switch                 | Swaps left and right
    how Swaps the left and right channels.
    sound Left and right trade places in the stereo image.
DcRemove  "DC removal"     0 1     0    switch                 | Removes DC offset: 2nd-order high-pass at 5 Hz (20 Hz passes within 0.02 dB)
    how Removes any constant offset with a gentle 5 Hz high-pass.
    sound Clicks and wasted headroom caused by DC offset disappear; the audible sound is unchanged.
group Matrix
Matrix    "Matrix"         0 2     0    enum Off Encode_M/S Decode_M/S | Mid/side for the machines between two Utilities. Encode M/S: after the other stages, the output carries mid (L + R)/2 on the left and side (L − R)/2 on the right. Decode M/S: before them, the input is read as mid and side and turned back into L = M + S, R = M − S. Off: left and right as they are
    how Turns left/right into mid/side (Encode) or back (Decode), for processing between two Utilities.
    sound Between an encode and a decode, a machine in the chain works on the centre and the sides separately.
